rix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a144d0a5-a3d7-5351-8252-660793920527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515581 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={